BT /F1 10 Tf 40 800 Td 12 TL (SOP-HW-04 Hot Work Permit Procedure) Tj T* (Revision 5. Effective 01 March 2026. Harbourline Marine Services yard procedures.) Tj T* (1. Purpose. This procedure defines the controls required before, during and after hot work \(welding, cutting,) Tj T* (2. Obtain a Hot Work Permit signed by the Permit Issuer and the Area Authority before any hot work starts. A p) Tj T* (3. Remove all flammable and combustible materials within 11 m \(35 ft\) of the hot work. Where removal is not ) Tj T* (4. Post a trained fire watch with a charged extinguisher for the full duration of hot work. The fire watch sha) Tj T* (5. Test the atmosphere for flammable gas before work starts in enclosed or confined spaces and at intervals no) Tj T* (6. Close the permit. On completion the Area Authority inspects the location and closes the permit. Hot surface) Tj T* (Definitions) Tj T* (Fire watch: Trained person who watches for fire during and after hot work.) Tj T* (Flash point: Lowest temperature at which a liquid gives off enough vapour to ignite.) Tj T* (Area Authority: Person responsible for the work area who inspects and closes the permit.) Tj T* (Permit Issuer: Supervisor authorised to issue a hot work permit.) Tj T* (Personal protective equipment: welding helmet or face shield, fire-resistant coveralls, gloves, safety boots. ) Tj T* ET
